WEBVTT

00:11.290 --> 00:12.730
This can't be happening.

00:12.730 --> 00:15.140
Let's see, milk, garbage bags,

00:15.140 --> 00:16.870
we still have rice...

00:16.870 --> 00:18.280
Please, no.

00:20.080 --> 00:24.070
"Claskey Klasky Gets in a Huge Fight,
and now they're breaking up..."

00:20.830 --> 00:25.120
Maybe?

00:23.960 --> 00:25.120
Possibly?

00:24.070 --> 00:24.800
"Maybe?"

00:26.230 --> 00:27.630
Breaking up? What?!

00:27.870 --> 00:29.450
I'm so done.

00:29.450 --> 00:32.070
What's even the point of my life anymore?

00:32.070 --> 00:33.260
Uh-huh.

00:33.520 --> 00:37.010
I can see it happening with those two.

00:37.530 --> 00:39.390
They were really at each other's throats

00:39.810 --> 00:42.510
at the girls' day out, remember?

00:43.300 --> 00:44.530
They'll get sick of each
other, and one day,

00:44.530 --> 00:46.810
before you even know it, she'll happen
to have a knife in her hand, and...

00:46.810 --> 00:47.860
Stab!

00:48.140 --> 00:49.150
One of those?

00:49.150 --> 00:50.910
No, I don't think it's <i>that</i> bad.

00:50.910 --> 00:53.250
"Web searches are rising fast,

00:53.250 --> 00:56.230
but there has yet to be
an official announcement."

00:56.230 --> 00:57.870
So there's still some hope.

00:57.870 --> 00:59.200
It's coming.

00:59.570 --> 01:01.790
I bet there's going to be
an official announcement soon.

01:02.030 --> 01:03.500
Stop!

01:05.630 --> 01:07.310
Life is busy.

01:07.920 --> 01:08.680
Forget about them.

01:08.680 --> 01:09.660
Cold turkey!

01:09.660 --> 01:10.670
Already?!

01:10.670 --> 01:12.920
These stories are often

01:13.310 --> 01:16.310
baseless rumors or just
flat-out wrong, though.

01:16.310 --> 01:18.020
Exactly. Don't be so awful.

01:18.020 --> 01:19.170
You're acquaintances, aren't you?

01:19.170 --> 01:21.090
Which is it?

01:31.280 --> 01:34.280
I'm truly sorry for all the trouble

01:34.280 --> 01:36.610
and worry we've caused.

01:38.010 --> 01:40.660
Claskey Klasky will be disbanding

01:40.660 --> 01:47.530
as of today!

01:40.780 --> 01:41.580
Disbanding as of today!

03:18.960 --> 03:20.260
Furgle!

03:19.090 --> 03:22.180
14: "Claskey Klasky Breaks Up,
Kanae Makes Her Debut"

03:20.960 --> 03:22.180
So it's true.

03:23.760 --> 03:25.390
Psyche!

03:25.390 --> 03:26.580
I'm rehearsing.

03:26.580 --> 03:27.560
Rehearsing?!

03:27.790 --> 03:28.680
So it was just practice?

03:29.130 --> 03:30.770
The real gig is coming up, though.

03:31.000 --> 03:32.060
What's wrong with you?

03:32.360 --> 03:34.900
So are you breaking up or not?

03:34.900 --> 03:35.560
Which is it?

03:38.130 --> 03:40.240
Lisz-chan!

03:40.640 --> 03:42.530
That man is so awful!

03:42.530 --> 03:44.950
He doesn't even treat me like a human being.

03:45.170 --> 03:46.570
What man?

03:46.570 --> 03:48.110
Wiggy McWigface?

03:48.110 --> 03:51.260
She's obviously talking
about Bach, her producer.

03:51.260 --> 03:52.890
That's who I mean.

03:53.460 --> 03:56.420
We're releasing a new song soon.

03:56.640 --> 04:00.510
"Claskey Klasky to introduce a new song
in a live performance this weekend."

04:00.510 --> 04:03.450
They took out my solo!

04:04.470 --> 04:05.300
I believe you.

04:05.600 --> 04:07.700
I practiced so hard,

04:07.700 --> 04:10.790
and I don't have a single part
where I get to sing by myself.

04:10.790 --> 04:12.610
An unrequited love.

04:13.260 --> 04:14.730
Dammit, Bąda!

04:14.730 --> 04:18.450
That talentless, hack, one-hit wonder

04:18.450 --> 04:21.070
couldn't do anything without me!

04:21.490 --> 04:23.110
Bąda-chan? A one-hit wonder?

04:23.450 --> 04:25.630
Yes, I told you before.

04:25.630 --> 04:28.860
Tekla Bądarzewska was a Polish composer who

04:28.860 --> 04:31.500
became world-famous with just one hit piece.

04:31.940 --> 04:35.610
Nowadays, she's called the one-hit wonder
of classical composers.

04:35.910 --> 04:36.950
Did you?

04:36.950 --> 04:37.960
What?!

04:38.460 --> 04:40.590
Expect anything of love,

04:41.280 --> 04:43.600
and you will receive nothing but tragedy.

04:45.650 --> 04:48.350
That could be a strategy,
though, couldn't it?

04:49.580 --> 04:53.540
Bach-san can be strict at times, but maybe

04:53.540 --> 04:57.350
the reasons for his actions
are clearer in the long term.

04:59.180 --> 05:02.300
Maybe there's a lot to think about when

05:02.300 --> 05:04.740
you're in a position of
responsibility as a musician.

05:04.740 --> 05:06.190
How?!

05:06.190 --> 05:09.280
How can you be so patronizing
on your way out the door?!

05:09.280 --> 05:11.510
What do you know about that man?

05:11.510 --> 05:13.500
I see him every day at work!

05:13.730 --> 05:16.420
H-He came over the other day.

05:16.420 --> 05:18.000
He came here?!

05:18.000 --> 05:18.820
Yeah.

05:18.820 --> 05:22.600
But we just talked and had tea.

05:23.140 --> 05:24.970
Keep talking shit,

05:24.970 --> 05:27.400
and I'll pound your mouth in, bitch!

05:27.400 --> 05:28.300
Talking shit? But...

05:29.000 --> 05:32.740
You need an interpreter for
him. All he ever says is,

05:32.740 --> 05:35.890
like, "A capriccio," or, "Poco a poco."

05:35.890 --> 05:37.080
Yup.

05:37.080 --> 05:40.800
Even I hadn't heard him speak
Japanese until the other day,

05:40.800 --> 05:43.260
when he finally said a little bit
and shocked the hell out of me.

05:43.260 --> 05:45.030
Actually, he was pretty chatty.

05:45.520 --> 05:46.820
Chatty.

05:46.820 --> 05:48.090
For, like, twenty minutes.

05:49.310 --> 05:52.910
He said, "Contact me if
you ever need anything."

05:56.110 --> 05:58.870
Impossible!

05:59.170 --> 06:01.540
Hold it, you aren't talking
out of your ass anymore!

06:01.930 --> 06:03.750
You don't know anything!

06:02.100 --> 06:04.550
It hurts! It hurts!

06:03.750 --> 06:05.850
Anything!

06:04.290 --> 06:06.140
No, Tchaiko, stop.

06:06.140 --> 06:08.370
There, there.

06:08.740 --> 06:12.530
That man needs me!

06:12.530 --> 06:14.240
That man...

06:14.240 --> 06:14.970
Yes, yes.

06:15.500 --> 06:18.790
I know. You were interpreting
for him all this time.

06:19.090 --> 06:20.980
Yet he never really needed it.

06:20.980 --> 06:22.480
Please don't say it.

06:22.970 --> 06:26.350
In fact, why didn't he ever
speak normally before?

06:26.350 --> 06:27.490
That's it!

06:28.970 --> 06:31.240
What a pain.

06:31.970 --> 06:34.320
I have to make dinner for one more.

06:34.870 --> 06:38.000
I wonder what would help
with Tchaiko-chan's nerves.

06:38.000 --> 06:40.370
Takamatsu Supermarket

06:38.700 --> 06:40.370
Russian food, I guess?

06:40.720 --> 06:42.570
Beef stroganoff,

06:42.840 --> 06:46.680
pirozhki, pot-au-feu, gazpacho?

06:46.680 --> 06:48.280
Gorbachev...

06:54.640 --> 06:58.640
Feel free to contact me if
there's anything you need.

07:07.880 --> 07:10.660
I wonder if my email annoyed him.

07:10.980 --> 07:13.300
Producers are busy, aren't they?

07:14.100 --> 07:16.780
I never thought they'd suddenly
call me over, though.

07:17.330 --> 07:18.630
I wonder why.

07:20.090 --> 07:21.220
Bąda-san?

07:21.220 --> 07:22.830
Thank you for coming!

07:23.430 --> 07:25.710
Hey, Tchaiko-chan's at my place right now...

07:25.710 --> 07:27.210
I look forward to working with you.

07:28.310 --> 07:30.980
Tchaiko's been treating me like
I'm an idiot this whole time.

07:30.980 --> 07:35.540
I can finally cut ties with that hot mess.

07:35.540 --> 07:38.270
We can have a fresh start together!

07:38.520 --> 07:39.980
Uh...

07:41.210 --> 07:42.380
Start what?

07:45.290 --> 07:47.600
Dude, Kanae, this is nuts.

07:47.940 --> 07:56.330
From: Kanae
Bąda-san's begging me to be an idol
with her, so I'm going to be home late.

07:48.330 --> 07:51.410
"Bąda-san's begging me
to be an idol with her,

07:51.410 --> 07:53.290
so I'm going to be home late."

07:53.290 --> 07:54.570
Man, she's so dull.

07:54.570 --> 07:56.590
Doesn't she know how to
use emojis or anything?

07:56.590 --> 07:57.910
Never mind that.

07:57.910 --> 07:59.750
She's been asked to

08:00.080 --> 08:02.040
take my job.

08:02.280 --> 08:04.160
Your job?! Now?

08:04.160 --> 08:05.540
<i>Our</i> Kanae?

08:06.360 --> 08:09.840
So then, did Bach talk to my little kitten?

08:10.210 --> 08:11.150
Yeah.

08:11.150 --> 08:14.660
Immediately finding a replacement
sounds like something he'd do.

08:16.040 --> 08:17.430
Let them do what they want.

08:17.770 --> 08:19.410
Are you really sure?

08:19.410 --> 08:20.720
I have to reply.

08:20.720 --> 08:22.810
"You should totally become an idol."

08:23.300 --> 08:26.010
Welcome death upon the girl's drab nature.

08:26.620 --> 08:28.820
Be reborn as an idol.

08:30.260 --> 08:31.210
Write that. Go.

08:31.900 --> 08:34.420
"Send me some photos.

08:34.420 --> 08:37.120
I'll make a post online."

08:37.350 --> 08:38.820
Well, hmm...

08:38.820 --> 08:41.660
Kanae's a hard sell, though.

08:41.660 --> 08:43.750
I wonder if Bach-kun can figure it out.

08:44.320 --> 08:48.320
Indeed, he gave up on selling
someone I happen to know.

08:52.330 --> 08:54.530
Wait, why is everyone agreeing?

08:54.530 --> 08:55.990
They're crazy.

08:55.990 --> 08:57.460
We'll make it huge, if we become a hit.

08:57.460 --> 08:59.020
It's a once-in-a-lifetime opportunity.

09:00.520 --> 09:01.850
Once-in-a-lifetime...

09:03.680 --> 09:05.940
All right, let's make a hit!

09:06.520 --> 09:08.430
No talking about making one hit!

09:08.430 --> 09:10.730
It bothers you <i>that</i> much?

09:12.100 --> 09:12.940
Dance!

09:12.940 --> 09:13.680
Voice!

09:13.680 --> 09:14.600
Walking!

09:14.600 --> 09:16.540
Heart-catching MC!

09:16.840 --> 09:19.810
We're going to turn you into an idol!

09:22.290 --> 09:23.950
Let's do this.

09:24.470 --> 09:26.780
Oh... Oh, no.

09:27.710 --> 09:31.590
"Common sense"
is just an excuse!!

09:27.710 --> 09:32.880
Operation Kanae Idol Promotion
Strategy Meeting

09:28.880 --> 09:32.880
A live venue for a top-class
idol in this day and age...

09:33.200 --> 09:35.400
Fukuoka Stadium. Nagoya Public Hall.

09:35.400 --> 09:37.510
Kyoto Plaza. Osaka Hall.

09:37.840 --> 09:39.890
Thus, we can expect...

09:40.270 --> 09:42.690
Pollock roe, miso katsu, yatsuhashi,

09:42.690 --> 09:44.520
and finally, okonomiyaki.

09:44.820 --> 09:46.900
What about the swimsuit contest?

09:47.380 --> 09:48.480
What's she going to stuff it with?

09:48.480 --> 09:49.440
We gotta hurry.

09:49.880 --> 09:52.440
With natural materials, like this.

09:52.840 --> 09:53.500
Like this?

09:53.500 --> 09:54.120
Like this?

09:54.120 --> 09:54.640
Like this.

09:54.640 --> 09:55.330
Like this!

09:55.330 --> 09:55.850
Like this.

09:55.850 --> 09:56.700
Like this!

09:56.990 --> 10:00.820
Why not change her less boring sentence
suffix, to give her some country girl appeal?

10:01.550 --> 10:02.950
That's it-eel!

10:02.950 --> 10:03.990
How's this-eel?

10:04.320 --> 10:06.960
"New idol making her debut."

10:07.810 --> 10:09.830
Oh yeah, we should ask Tchaiko-chan

10:09.830 --> 10:12.030
for her opinion, since
she knows this industry.

10:12.330 --> 10:13.670
Where'd she go?

10:19.330 --> 10:23.330
Man, I feel so much comfier
dressed like this.

10:23.330 --> 10:25.100
It's been a while.

10:25.610 --> 10:27.130
She's in old fart mode.

10:27.660 --> 10:31.390
Tch-Tchaiko-chan?

10:49.290 --> 10:51.690
This'll make for a good experiment.

10:53.190 --> 10:54.330
I get it.

10:54.870 --> 10:57.970
You think this landlady might be the key to

10:58.320 --> 11:01.080
the relationship between that
bizarre mansion and Musik.

11:04.870 --> 11:07.850
All right, now, follow my lead.

11:11.630 --> 11:12.460
Go.

11:20.830 --> 11:23.070
Why do I have to be an idol?

11:23.660 --> 11:24.540
No.

11:24.540 --> 11:26.490
Leaky roof, insulation upgrades,

11:26.490 --> 11:29.240
sewer pipe replacement,
rust-proofing, painting costs...

11:30.210 --> 11:32.290
001: Beethes-san
Be reborn
002: Beethes-san
Die once
003: Beethes-san
What's wrong?!
004: Beethes-san
Tragedy awaits your awakening
005: Beethes-san
Sign proposal 3

11:30.500 --> 11:32.270
What's with all these messages?

11:33.080 --> 11:34.250
Proposal: End your sentences with -eel
How are you-eel?
Eel all your sentences with "eel!"
Hashtag eel!

11:36.550 --> 11:38.050
Make it racy!
Show off your ass!

11:40.370 --> 11:42.440
Nein!

11:52.280 --> 11:53.930
My tummy...

11:53.930 --> 11:56.520
I'm so hungry.

11:56.860 --> 11:58.170
Kanae...

11:58.170 --> 12:01.150
When are you coming home?

12:01.590 --> 12:03.570
We're out of gyoza, too.

12:04.180 --> 12:05.990
Don't we have anything?

12:08.270 --> 12:09.580
This'll do.

12:12.320 --> 12:13.370
It's mine.

12:15.720 --> 12:16.810
Underage!

12:17.320 --> 12:19.980
We've not a single drop of beer
to give to a child.

12:19.980 --> 12:21.360
Then I'll—

12:21.360 --> 12:22.760
None for adults, either.

12:22.980 --> 12:24.100
Fine.

12:23.390 --> 12:25.450
Oh, come on!

12:24.100 --> 12:26.870
I'm not an idol anymore.

12:25.450 --> 12:28.220
Please, I'm a grown-up.

12:27.430 --> 12:29.110
I'll do whatever I please!

12:31.560 --> 12:33.220
Vodka is made from plants

12:33.220 --> 12:35.690
such as rye and potatoes.

12:35.990 --> 12:38.500
It is fermented, and then it is

12:38.500 --> 12:41.880
distilled for its alcohol content.

12:42.830 --> 12:44.450
Don't tell me...

12:45.270 --> 12:46.190
You're joking.

13:08.930 --> 13:12.890
In Japan, it is illegal to produce

13:12.890 --> 13:14.980
alcoholic beverages without permission.

13:16.120 --> 13:18.150
It's illegal.

13:18.530 --> 13:21.810
You have to distract
yourself with something.

13:22.250 --> 13:23.220
I get it.

13:23.540 --> 13:25.450
Mail from Mitsuru-san.

13:25.450 --> 13:26.690
It's the agency.

13:29.120 --> 13:31.200
I can't take it anymore

13:31.490 --> 13:33.590
I can't take it anymore

13:33.890 --> 13:35.850
I can't take it anymore

13:35.850 --> 13:38.250
I seriously, seriously can't

13:38.580 --> 13:40.370
I can't even

13:40.370 --> 13:40.880
Nope

13:40.880 --> 13:42.630
I can't even

13:42.480 --> 13:43.090
Her face!

13:42.630 --> 13:43.090
Nope

13:43.520 --> 13:44.920
Her face!

13:44.920 --> 13:47.170
That's the face of a hard worker.

13:46.980 --> 13:48.280
Her face!

13:47.170 --> 13:49.850
You've become such a man, Kanae.

13:49.850 --> 13:51.690
What have you become?

13:51.420 --> 13:52.730
Her face!

13:51.690 --> 13:53.800
She definitely doesn't look like an idol.

13:55.860 --> 13:58.650
It isn't easy being an idol.

13:58.650 --> 14:00.590
There's an article attached.

14:01.000 --> 14:03.610
"Tchaiko will be absent at the PR live event

14:03.610 --> 14:06.560
promoting the new Claskey Klasky
song at Hamamatsu Records

14:03.610 --> 14:07.610
Claskey Klasky to have a new member?

14:03.610 --> 14:07.610
Tchaiko will be absent from the
PR live event promoting the new
Claskey Klasky song at
Hamamatsu Records this Sunday,
due to health issues.

14:06.560 --> 14:08.850
this Sunday, due to health issues.

14:08.850 --> 14:12.200
Bąda is expected to bring the

14:12.200 --> 14:16.010
highly-anticipated new member
on stage. Don't miss it!"

14:16.010 --> 14:17.700
Highly-anticipated newcomer?

14:17.700 --> 14:18.750
Me?

14:19.470 --> 14:21.730
My little kitten's making her debut!

14:21.730 --> 14:24.170
Holy crap! Oh, man!

14:24.170 --> 14:25.660
This'll be a sight to see.

14:25.660 --> 14:27.050
We should all go see her.

14:27.800 --> 14:29.930
It's me, right? It's me, right?

14:38.100 --> 14:39.140
Be careful.

14:39.610 --> 14:41.480
We have our show tomorrow.

14:41.480 --> 14:44.030
Your pants are so long, Bąda-chan.

14:44.030 --> 14:46.860
Our legs aren't the same
length. What can I do?

14:46.860 --> 14:48.280
You're terrible.

14:48.990 --> 14:50.490
Whatever, let's get some sleep.

14:55.030 --> 14:56.090
Don't worry.

14:56.450 --> 14:58.340
It'll work out with the two of us.

14:59.120 --> 15:00.470
I can tell.

15:01.510 --> 15:03.320
When I was with Tchaiko,

15:03.780 --> 15:05.910
I was always the moon.

15:06.460 --> 15:08.220
Tchaiko was the sun.

15:08.540 --> 15:11.120
She was always the one in the spotlight.

15:12.270 --> 15:16.270
But with you, I feel like it'll be like

15:16.890 --> 15:19.940
there're two suns, warming everyone up.

15:19.940 --> 15:21.950
We can form a cozy unit together.

15:22.550 --> 15:24.070
I can feel it.

15:25.220 --> 15:27.720
Maybe that man set it all up so

15:28.020 --> 15:31.560
we would meet each other again.

15:33.600 --> 15:34.770
Are you asleep?

15:35.990 --> 15:37.730
I was listening.

15:37.730 --> 15:39.200
I wasn't thinking about
my autograph or anything.

15:40.300 --> 15:41.860
Seriously, go to sleep.

15:45.590 --> 15:55.600
[Viewer Beware] Tchaiko's replacement
is terrible [Bąda loses hope]
 Tags: -Claskey Klasky -Epic fail -Umad? -Out of their minds

15:45.910 --> 15:48.390
"Damn, that new girl's scary lol"

15:46.050 --> 15:47.380
Damn, that new girl's scary lol

15:47.380 --> 15:48.090
omg her face

15:48.130 --> 15:50.800
She's snapped lolol

15:48.340 --> 15:51.010
Hilarious

15:48.390 --> 15:49.900
"She's snapped."

15:49.670 --> 15:53.800
Snapadoll? lol

15:49.900 --> 15:50.800
"Snapadoll?"

15:51.010 --> 15:52.890
"Snapadoll, lol. Snap, snap."

15:52.890 --> 15:53.800
"I'll go check them out tomorrow."

15:53.930 --> 15:55.600
"That's hilarious. Snap, snap."

15:56.320 --> 15:59.930
Setting us up the bomb.

16:06.190 --> 16:08.030
Shall I heat it up for you?

16:08.410 --> 16:10.740
Your hearts, to go!

16:10.740 --> 16:13.150
A little sun to warm you up!

16:13.150 --> 16:15.360
I'm Kanae!

16:16.620 --> 16:17.910
I'm...

16:18.780 --> 16:21.310
I'm...

16:23.130 --> 16:24.210
It's no use.

16:26.860 --> 16:28.110
What do I do?

16:28.110 --> 16:30.390
I'm getting really nervous all of a sudden.

16:30.390 --> 16:31.960
Here's something good to know.

16:33.190 --> 16:35.000
Just pretend everyone

16:35.000 --> 16:37.550
in the audience is watching me.

16:37.960 --> 16:39.530
Oh, right.

16:39.530 --> 16:42.600
They wouldn't know anything about me.

16:42.870 --> 16:44.100
Exactly.

16:44.100 --> 16:45.480
So just relax,

16:46.110 --> 16:47.810
you'll be fine.

16:47.810 --> 16:48.900
Right.

16:48.900 --> 16:50.860
Kanana!

16:50.860 --> 16:52.780
Snapadoll! Snapadoll! Get mad!

16:52.780 --> 16:53.820
Bring it, Snapadoll!

16:53.820 --> 16:55.360
Scold me!

16:55.360 --> 16:57.290
Snapadoll!

16:57.540 --> 16:59.080
Get mad!

16:59.080 --> 17:00.940
Kanana!

17:00.940 --> 17:02.540
Scold me!

17:03.410 --> 17:05.410
This isn't what you promised.

17:06.040 --> 17:07.700
Kanana!

17:07.160 --> 17:09.290
They're calling you Kanana.

17:09.290 --> 17:10.530
That's cute.

17:11.410 --> 17:13.840
Snap for making a mess in my room!

17:13.840 --> 17:15.340
Kanana!

17:15.610 --> 17:18.010
Snap for the tearing the wallpaper!

17:18.270 --> 17:19.560
Kanana!

17:19.860 --> 17:21.770
Snap! Snapadoll!

17:22.070 --> 17:24.730
Go, Kanana!

17:24.730 --> 17:53.840
Snapadoll! Snapadoll!

17:28.100 --> 17:29.860
It's love.

17:30.340 --> 17:31.990
How could this be happening?

17:31.990 --> 17:32.970
Why?

17:33.270 --> 17:34.900
Why is Kanae getting all the attention?

17:34.900 --> 17:37.080
Am I only the moon,

17:37.080 --> 17:39.570
even without Tchaiko around?

17:39.570 --> 17:40.660
It's time.

17:41.080 --> 17:42.200
Please.

17:42.980 --> 17:43.730
I can't.

17:43.730 --> 17:45.490
Come on. Be strong, Kanae.

17:45.490 --> 17:46.830
I can't! I'm scared.

17:46.830 --> 17:47.950
You can do it.

17:47.950 --> 17:49.380
We practiced so much.

17:50.510 --> 17:53.840
I want to go back to being a normal girl.

17:56.810 --> 17:59.090
This girl's different than me.

17:59.470 --> 18:00.650
She'll never make it,

18:01.730 --> 18:03.810
even once.

18:06.120 --> 18:07.430
That's it.

18:07.430 --> 18:09.310
They call me a one-hit wonder,

18:09.310 --> 18:11.740
but how many people in the world

18:11.740 --> 18:14.030
make it even once?

18:15.220 --> 18:19.110
I'll show them what this
one-hit wonder's made of.

18:21.980 --> 18:23.660
Thanks, Kanae.

18:24.850 --> 18:26.020
It's okay.

18:26.020 --> 18:27.570
I can do it by myself.

18:27.870 --> 18:28.930
Bąda-san...

18:33.020 --> 18:34.000
Here they come.

18:34.300 --> 18:34.960
Huh?

18:35.350 --> 18:37.000
Where's my little kitten?

18:39.380 --> 18:41.700
Maybe she's too freaked out to show up.

18:41.700 --> 18:44.500
That's why we warmed up
the audience for her.

18:44.500 --> 18:46.430
What an inconsiderate girl.

18:46.820 --> 18:47.830
Where's Kanana?

18:54.580 --> 18:55.740
Tchaiko.

18:59.390 --> 19:00.570
Bądarzewska.

19:01.970 --> 19:03.780
Tchaikovsky.

19:04.710 --> 19:05.620
Nope.

19:05.930 --> 19:07.290
Don't come up here.

19:07.680 --> 19:09.850
It's finally my time.

19:10.240 --> 19:12.820
I'm the only sun.

19:12.820 --> 19:13.410
Wait.

19:13.410 --> 19:14.120
No.

19:15.430 --> 19:19.310
You're too late.

19:20.820 --> 19:24.810
Ja gram. Ja modlę się.

19:37.870 --> 19:42.890
Some days it'll rain

19:42.670 --> 19:44.250
Watch me.

19:43.880 --> 19:48.890
Some days it'll snow

19:45.400 --> 19:47.310
Watch only me.

19:47.970 --> 19:50.250
Here I am.

19:49.870 --> 19:54.880
Some days I may cry

19:50.590 --> 19:52.610
It's so warm.

19:53.220 --> 19:57.170
This is Tekla Bądarzewska's sole hit piece,

19:55.170 --> 20:01.090
Some days are ridiculously fun

19:58.350 --> 20:00.190
"A Maiden's Prayer."

20:00.630 --> 20:03.340
Wait for me!

20:03.340 --> 20:04.050
Go away!

20:04.660 --> 20:06.610
I'm going to shine by myself.

20:07.110 --> 20:10.390
There's only one sun in my universe.

20:10.980 --> 20:12.690
You don't get it.

20:12.690 --> 20:14.980
It's the countless, nameless stars that

20:15.350 --> 20:18.900
paint the universe which
spin around the sun.

20:19.590 --> 20:21.860
You need the moon, too.

20:23.090 --> 20:25.990
You think you have the right
to talk about the universe?

20:26.290 --> 20:28.160
Do you think you're God now? Is that it?

20:28.160 --> 20:29.100
No.

20:29.100 --> 20:30.920
I want to make music together with you.

20:30.920 --> 20:31.750
That's all.

20:31.980 --> 20:35.980
That man you abandoned was the god of music.

20:35.980 --> 20:38.080
No, I understand it now.

20:38.080 --> 20:39.340
It's our sound.

20:39.340 --> 20:41.280
It's the music we make
together that matters.

20:41.280 --> 20:43.990
That man made that music.

20:43.990 --> 20:46.710
You made such an effort to

20:46.710 --> 20:48.400
touch your fan's hearts, too.

20:49.310 --> 20:53.030
I don't know if people really
appreciate our work.

20:57.400 --> 21:00.410
Not even that man could create that desire.

21:00.410 --> 21:02.600
It's ours alone.

21:04.990 --> 21:08.170
It's ours, and it's real.

21:10.340 --> 21:11.680
Tchaiko-chan...

21:13.010 --> 21:15.080
You've been using my cleansing foam

21:15.520 --> 21:17.840
without asking me, haven't you?

21:18.310 --> 21:24.220
You knew?!

21:20.540 --> 21:21.800
I thought so.

21:25.870 --> 21:27.130
One go.

21:27.640 --> 21:29.890
A one-hit wonder's gotta do it in one go.

21:30.200 --> 21:33.850
I'm going to become the only sun!

21:37.020 --> 21:38.800
We're not worthy!

21:38.800 --> 21:40.780
We're not worthy!

21:41.160 --> 21:47.960
We're not worthy!

21:51.760 --> 21:53.330
Bądarzewska.

21:54.150 --> 21:56.530
Her Musik exceeded expectations, did it not?

21:57.050 --> 21:59.630
Odd goods, but good goods.

22:04.700 --> 22:06.880
We're not worthy!

22:07.720 --> 22:09.850
We're not worthy!

22:08.560 --> 22:10.660
You're amazing, Bąda-chan.

22:10.960 --> 22:12.200
Congrats.

22:17.310 --> 22:20.400
I saw your show, Bąda-san. It was godly.

22:20.400 --> 22:21.920
Where's our Kanana?

22:21.920 --> 22:24.900
The awakening of genius is
fraught with sacrifice.

22:25.550 --> 22:29.400
Wow, I never knew Bąda had such Musik.

22:30.010 --> 22:32.180
So, what are you going to do now?

22:39.470 --> 22:41.410
Shit...

22:42.070 --> 22:44.680
We're not worthy!

22:43.000 --> 22:46.010
To be continued

24:15.970 --> 24:25.060
Episode 15: School
Festival From Hell

24:16.580 --> 24:19.860
What does it mean to be serious? What is
youth? What is it to want to be popular?

24:19.860 --> 24:22.470
Is it to bleed, to starve,
to have bags under your eyes,

24:22.470 --> 24:23.940
and to realize you are
nonetheless forever alone?

24:23.940 --> 24:27.190
That there is but one person that is you?

24:27.190 --> 24:29.230
Kagura Sousuke, 16 years old.
